      "sequence_position": 13,
      "problem": "$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ 8 & 0 \\\\ 7 & -4\\end{aligned}],\\,[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSuppose $B$ and $C$ are bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W,$ respectively. The matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the linear map $T:V\\to W$ relative to these bases, and the coordinates of the vector $x\\in V$ relative to $B$ are shown above. Find $[T(x)]_{C}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The coordinates of the image of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ 8 & 0 \\\\ 7 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}17 \\\\ -24 \\\\ -25\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
